{
  "slug": "oi",
  "title_en": "Understanding the Open Interest Board: Where Smart Money Is Stacked",
  "excerpt_en": "Ranked by open interest—the inventory of outstanding contracts. Heavy OI strikes often act as support and resistance.",
  "body_en": "<style>\n  .aji-guide{\n    --bg:#f5f2f0; --ink:#151617; --gold:#c9a227;\n    --card:#fffdfb; --line:#e7e1d8; --muted:#6f6a63; --soft:#c9c2b6;\n    background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);\n    font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,\"Segoe UI\",\"PingFang SC\",\"Microsoft YaHei\",sans-serif;\n    line-height:1.75; font-size:16px; padding:4px;\n  }\n  .aji-guide h2{font-size:22px;margin:0 0 10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.2px}\n  .aji-guide h3{font-size:18px;margin:26px 0 8px;font-weight:700}\n  .aji-guide p{margin:10px 0}\n  .aji-guide .lead{font-size:17px}\n  .aji-guide .accent{color:var(--gold);font-weight:700}\n  .aji-guide .chart-card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 22px;margin:22px 0;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(21,22,23,.05)}\n  .aji-guide .chart-note{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:6px 0 14px}\n  .aji-guide canvas{max-width:100%}\n  .aji-guide .analogy{border-left:4px solid var(--gold);background:rgba(201,162,39,.07);padding:12px 16px;border-radius:0 10px 10px 0;margin:16px 0}\n  .aji-guide .data-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:14.5px;overflow:hidden;border-radius:10px}\n  .aji-guide .data-table th{background:var(--ink);color:#f5f2f0;text-align:left;padding:11px 14px;font-weight:600}\n  .aji-guide .data-table td{padding:11px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}\n  .aji-guide .data-table tr:nth-child(even) td{background:rgba(201,162,39,.035)}\n  .aji-guide .data-table .col{font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);white-space:nowrap}\n  .aji-guide .tag{display:inline-block;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:20px}\n  .aji-guide .tag-core{background:var(--gold);color:#fff}\n  .aji-guide .tag-base{background:var(--soft);color:var(--ink)}\n  .aji-guide .disclaimer{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:26px;padding-top:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}\n  .aji-guide .cta{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;background:var(--gold);color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-weight:700;padding:11px 20px;border-radius:10px;font-size:15px;box-shadow:0 2px 6px rgba(201,162,39,.3);transition:background .15s}\n  .aji-guide .cta:hover{background:#b8911f}\n  .aji-guide .cta-row{margin:16px 0 4px}\n  .aji-guide .cta-bottom{background:rgba(201,162,39,.08);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:18px 20px;margin:24px 0 8px;text-align:center}\n  .aji-guide .cta-bottom p{margin:0 0 10px;font-weight:700}\n</style>\n\n<div class=\"aji-guide\">\n  <h2>Understanding the Open Interest Board: Where Smart Money Is Stacked</h2>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Ranked by <span class=\"accent\">open interest (OI), highest first</span>. Volume is today's flow; OI is the reservoir—where the market has <b>stacked the most contracts</b>, often becoming support and resistance.</p>\n  <div class=\"cta-row\"><a class=\"cta\" href=\"https://www.options-aji.com/options/open-interest\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">📊 Open live Open Interest board →</a></div>\n  <h3>1. What Is Open Interest?</h3>\n  <div class=\"analogy\"><p style=\"margin:4px 0\"><b>OI = open contracts not yet closed.</b></p><p style=\"margin:4px 0\">New matched pairs add OI; closes subtract. It's <b>accumulated inventory</b>.</p><p style=\"margin:8px 0 4px\"><span class=\"accent\">This board shows where inventory concentrates.</span></p></div>\n  <div class=\"chart-card\"><h2 style=\"font-size:18px\">OI by Strike: Position Walls (example)</h2><p class=\"chart-note\">Call/Put OI by strike. Heavy walls magnetize price. Rendered with Chart.js via jsDelivr CDN only.</p><canvas id=\"ajiOiWall\" width=\"640\" height=\"300\" aria-label=\"OI by strike chart\"></canvas></div>\n  <p>Call walls act as ceilings; put walls as floors—dealer hedging creates magnet + resistance, the intuition behind <span class=\"accent\">Max Pain</span>.</p>\n  <h3>2. Watch ΔOI, Not Just Level OI</h3>\n  <p>Rising <span class=\"accent\">ΔOI</span> = new builds; falling ΔOI = unwinds—often more actionable than absolute OI.</p>\n  <div class=\"chart-card\"><h2 style=\"font-size:18px\">Today's ΔOI</h2><p class=\"chart-note\">Gold = net new positioning; gray = net closes.</p><canvas id=\"ajiOiDelta\" width=\"640\" height=\"280\" aria-label=\"OI change chart\"></canvas></div>\n  <h3>3. Column Guide</h3>\n  <table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>Column</th><th>Meaning</th><th>How to use</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">#</td><td>Rank by OI.</td><td>Heavier inventory.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">Contract</td><td>Symbol, expiry, strike, side.</td><td>OI clusters = battle lines.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">OI <span class=\"tag tag-core\">Core</span></td><td>Open contracts.</td><td>Map vs stock for S/R.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">ΔOI</td><td>Day-over-day OI change.</td><td><span class=\"accent\">+ build / − close</span>.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">Volume</td><td>Today's volume.</td><td>High vol, flat OI = churn.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">Turnover</td><td>Notional premium.</td><td>Size of participation.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">IV <span class=\"tag tag-base\">Aux</span></td><td>Implied vol.</td><td>Event bets on heavy strikes.</td></tr>\n  <tr><td class=\"col\">Chg <span class=\"tag tag-base\">Aux</span></td><td>Contract price change.</td><td>Pair with ΔOI.</td></tr>\n  </tbody></table>\n  <h3>4. Three Reminders</h3>\n  <p><b>1. High OI ≠ direction.</b> Read ΔOI and price together.<br><b>2. OI is slow</b>—usually prior close.<br><b>3. Pinning strengthens near expiry.</b></p>\n  <div class=\"cta-bottom\"><p>Ready to explore? See today's live data 👇</p><a class=\"cta\" href=\"https://www.options-aji.com/options/open-interest\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">📊 Open live Open Interest board →</a></div><p class=\"disclaimer\">Data may be delayed ~15 minutes. For research only—not investment advice. Options trading involves substantial risk of loss. © OptionsAji</p>\n\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/chart.js@4.4.1/dist/chart.umd.min.js\"></script>\n<script>\n(function(){\n  if (typeof Chart === 'undefined') return;\n  var GOLD='#c9a227', GOLD_SOFT='rgba(201,162,39,.85)', GRAY='#c9c2b6', INK='#151617';\n\n  var strikes=['120','130','140','150','160','170'];\n  var callOi=[15000,22000,48000,60000,35000,40000];\n  var putOi=[40000,55000,38000,20000,12000,8000];\n  var c1=document.getElementById('ajiOiWall');\n  if(c1){ new Chart(c1,{type:'bar',data:{labels:strikes,datasets:[\n      {label:'Call OI',data:callOi,backgroundColor:GOLD_SOFT,borderRadius:4},\n      {label:'Put OI',data:putOi,backgroundColor:GRAY,borderRadius:4}]},\n    options:{responsive:true,plugins:{legend:{labels:{color:INK,font:{size:13}}},\n      tooltip:{callbacks:{label:function(i){return i.dataset.label+'：'+i.parsed.y.toLocaleString()+' contracts';},title:function(t){return 'Strike $'+t[0].label;}}}},\n      scales:{x:{title:{display:true,text:'Strike',color:INK},ticks:{color:INK},grid:{display:false}},\n        y:{ticks:{color:INK,callback:function(v){return (v/1000)+'k';}},grid:{color:'rgba(21,22,23,.06)'}}}}}); }\n\n  var dLabels=['NVDA C','TSLA P','SPY C','AAPL C','AMD P'];\n  var dOi=[18000,12000,-9000,7000,-6000];\n  var c2=document.getElementById('ajiOiDelta');\n  if(c2){ new Chart(c2,{type:'bar',data:{labels:dLabels,datasets:[{label:'ΔOI',data:dOi,\n      backgroundColor:dOi.map(function(v){return v>=0?GOLD:GRAY;}),borderRadius:4}]},\n    options:{responsive:true,plugins:{legend:{display:false},\n      tooltip:{callbacks:{label:function(i){return (i.parsed.y>=0?'Net build +':'Net close ')+i.parsed.y.toLocaleString()+' contracts';}}}},\n      scales:{x:{ticks:{color:INK},grid:{display:false}},\n        y:{ticks:{color:INK,callback:function(v){return (v/1000)+'k';}},grid:{color:'rgba(21,22,23,.06)'}}}}}); }\n})();\n</script>"
}
